# Code Quality Standards

> **Note**: These rules complement `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`. When instructions conflict, priority is: Direct user request > Runtime safety > AGENTS.md > Cursor rules. These rules are meant to guide, not constrain—iterate and adapt as the project evolves.

## Iteration & Flexibility

- Rules are guidelines, not absolutes—exceptions are acceptable when justified
- When patterns change, update the rules to reflect new best practices
- If a rule conflicts with a better approach, discuss and update rather than blindly follow

## Python Linting

- Use Ruff for Python linting: `python -m ruff check --no-cache api services scripts tests`
- Fix lint errors before marking work complete
- Use `--fix` flag for safe autofixes: `python -m ruff check --no-cache --fix api services scripts tests`

## TypeScript/ESLint

- Run `cd frontend && npm run typecheck` for type checking (or `npx tsc --noEmit`)
- Run `cd frontend && npm run lint` for ESLint checks
- Fix all errors before marking work complete
- Note: `tsc` and ESLint use different parsers — a file can pass one and fail the other
- **CI automatically runs type checks** via GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) on every push/PR

## Verification Before Completion

- Run relevant tests (`pytest` for Python, `npm run test:run` for frontend)
- Run lint checks for changed files
- Validate behavior of changed paths
- Confirm no avoidable regressions

## Code Organization

- **Backend**: `api/` for FastAPI routes, `services/` for business logic, `scripts/` for one-time setup
- **Frontend**: `pages/` for routes, `components/` for reusable UI, `lib/` for pure logic, `hooks/` for React hooks
- Keep pure logic modules free of React imports
- Extract reusable logic into shared modules

## Documentation

- Add concise docstrings for functions/classes
- Keep comments focused on "why," not "what"
- Maintain clear README and project docs

## Error Handling

- Use structured try/catch blocks
- Log detailed errors internally; show friendly messages to users
- Implement consistent error handling patterns
- Never expose sensitive information in errors

## Security

- Sanitize all user inputs
- Use parameterized queries (PostGIS queries use `%s` placeholders)
- Store sensitive tokens securely (env vars, not hardcoded)
- Enable HTTPS for all connections in production
- Follow data minimization principles
